./data/input_representation_atlas_crop_crossvalidation_2026-07-12/post_role_scope_adjudication_manifest.json:3239:          "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nFigure type: schematic workflow/prompt-design panel for biomedical NLP relation/function inference.\n\nVisible panels and labels: left panel titled “Gene-Protein Contexts” with sections “Gene-Protein relations,” “Protein function inferring,” and “Gene function inferring.” It shows task prompts, inputs, and outputs using placeholders such as `{Gene-entity}`, `{Pro-entity}`, `{G-function}`, `{Protein-function}`, and `{Gene-function}`. Right panel titled “Instances” gives an example with Pro-entity “Vacuolar protein sorting-associated protein 41 homolog,” Gene-entity “VPS41,” G-function text, and Protein-function text.\n\nQuantity measured or shown: no quantitative data or axes; it illustrates prompt templates and a concrete biomedical text instance for gene-protein/function extraction or inference.\n\nMain visible finding: the figure demonstrates how gene function summaries and protein function summaries can be used in prompt-based tasks to infer gene-protein relationships, possible gene products, and corresponding protein or gene functions."
