./data/input_representation_atlas_crop_crossvalidation_2026-07-12/input_role_adjudication_manifest.json:4700:        "caption": "Extended Data Fig. 1: Definition of different evaluators or scorers. For the scorer focusing on truthfulness, we evaluate the matching level of model outputs for the description of gene properties and gene functions. For the scorer focusing on structural correctness, we evaluate the correctness of the structure of model outputs by comparing them to the limitations in the prompt. The logos of scorers are generated by DALLE (OpenAI, 2024).",
./data/input_representation_atlas_crop_crossvalidation_2026-07-12/input_role_adjudication_manifest.json:4702:          "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nWorkflow/scoring schematic. The panel is labeled “Scorer” and shows two grader components: “Grader for truthfulness” and “Grader for structural correctness.” Each takes a green input box labeled “The function of gene...” and points via arrows to evaluation outcomes.\n\nIt illustrates scoring criteria rather than experimental data: correct gene names/functions receive a high truthfulness score, wrong gene names/functions receive a low score; correct output format receives a high structural score, wrong output format receives a low score. No axes, quantitative plots, biological measurements, or experimental results are shown."
./data/input_representation_atlas_crop_crossvalidation_2026-07-12/input_role_adjudication_manifest.json:4718:          "SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nTwo-panel schematic/instruction example for a biomedical LLM task. Panels labeled **a** and **b** show user prompts in blue boxes and LLM answers in peach boxes. Panel **a** includes a protein structure image and asks for the protein name; the LLM answer is “AF-O43280-F1.” Panel **b** includes a histology/microscopy image and asks whether gene **APOC1** is a marker gene of **macrophage** cell type; the LLM answer is “Yes.” The figure illustrates multimodal biomedical question-answering examples rather than quantitative experimental results."
